      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence identifies two shortcomings (overconfidence and incomplete/truncated transcriptions with language models) and details proposed solutions: neighborhood label smoothing (extending uniform/unigram smoothing) to reduce overconfidence and increase entropy, and controlling/constraining EOS emission during beam search (e.g., emitting EOS only within a narrow probability range from the most probable token) to prevent truncated transcripts, along with temperature adjustments. This directly addresses the question."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 2692.1245999401435
    },
    {
      "stage": "Generate",
      "attempt": 1,
      "input": {
